linaudit (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * SSH (static parse, without sshd -T): an Include directory or file that
    exists but cannot be read (permission denied, symlink loop) is now
    reported as skipped, so the settings it could set are shown as
    undetermined instead of passing on sshd defaults. A missing Include
    target is still ignored, as sshd does.

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@lexiworks.dev>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:58:50 -0300

linaudit (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release.
  * PAT-008: report CVEs without a fix yet in enabled network services
    (Apache, nginx, OpenSSH, Postfix, PostgreSQL...), using debsecan and the
    Debian security tracker. N/A when debsecan is not installed.
  * PER-012: decode the taint mask into its flags and list the modules that
    tainted the kernel, e.g. "tainted=12801 (P W O E): nvidia(POE), ...".
  * SSH (static parse, without sshd -T): follow sshd's Include precedence.
    Includes expand in place and the first value wins, Match only ends the
    file it appears in, paths resolve inside the audited root, and skipped
    files make settings undetermined instead of a false PASS (GitHub #14).
  * Score: a check module that crashes now marks the run incomplete and caps
    the score at 6/10, instead of silently dropping a whole category
    (GitHub #11).
  * debian/control: suggest debsecan.

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@lexiworks.dev>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:15:33 -0300

linaudit (0.2.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * FS-017: only list directories that are world-writable without the sticky
    bit; any directory with an orphan uid/gid was being reported (GitHub #4).
  * PER-013: exclude linaudit's own process (and its parent, matched by
    dev+inode) from the check (GitHub #10).
  * SEC-001/SEC-008: do not flag Lynis profile path rules as credentials
    (GitHub #9).
  * Refuse to write --output to anything other than a regular file
    (symlink, FIFO, device, directory) (GitHub #8).
  * FS-013..FS-018: skip backup snapshot trees (/timeshift, /timeshift-btrfs,
    /.snapshots); new FS-019 checks that they are not accessible to other
    users instead (GitHub #1).
  * FS-014: check every SUID/SGID file against the dpkg index; the fixed limit
    of 150 could leave /usr out when many paths sorted before it (GitHub #1).
  * FS-018: group orphan files under their topmost orphan directory, showing
    uid:gid and the number of entries (GitHub #1).

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@lexiworks.dev>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:54:01 -0300

linaudit (0.2.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * APP-050/APP-051: detect Apache by its main config file (apache2.conf /
    httpd.conf) instead of the /etc/apache2 directory, which javascript-common
    creates on Debian without Apache installed (false positive).

 -- Alexia Michelle <alexia@lexiworks.dev>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:34:04 -0300

